</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Slides <em id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">vs.</em> LLM Chat-based Learning</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section contains the questionnaire and results for User Study 2 (§<a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3. User Study 2: Comparing Slides and LLM Chat-based Learning from Learners’ Perspective ‣ 4. Experiments ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>), which compared slide-based learning with LLM chat-based learning on a controlled set of HCI research papers.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Rubric.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The comparative questionnaire items (Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Evaluation Rubric. ‣ A.3. Slides vs. LLM Chat-based Learning ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) directly contrast the two learning methods across five dimensions: visual clarity, structural clarity, support for understanding, engagement, and overall satisfaction.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8. </span>Questionnaire items comparing the slide-based format to participants’ typical LLM chat-based learning experience (7-point Likert scale: 1 = Strongly Disagree, 7 = Strongly Agree).</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T8.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T8.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T8.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:75.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T8.4.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation Dimension</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A1.T8.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:251.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Specific Assessment Items</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T8.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:75.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T8.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Visual Clarity and Intuitiveness</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T8.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:251.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format makes it easier for me to understand the paper because of its diagrams, images, and visual elements.</span></span>
<span id="A1.T8.4.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format provides more intuitive explanations of key concepts than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:75.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T8.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Structural Clarity and Organization</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T8.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:251.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format presents the paper’s information in a clearer and more logically organized structure than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
<span id="A1.T8.4.3.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format helps me more quickly build an overall understanding of the paper compared with the LLM chat format.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:75.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T8.4.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Learning Flow and Engagement</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T8.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:251.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format keeps my attention more focused during the learning process than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
<span id="A1.T8.4.4.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format offers a smoother and more natural flow for learning than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.4.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:75.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T8.4.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Support for Understanding and Memory</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T8.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:251.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format makes it easier for me to remember key concepts and details than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
<span id="A1.T8.4.5.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•The slide-based format helps me grasp the core ideas of the paper in less time than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T8.4.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T8.4.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:75.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T8.4.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Overall Satisfaction and Future Preference</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A1.T8.4.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.9pt 4.0pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:251.9pt;">
<span id="A1.T8.4.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•I find the slide-based format more enjoyable and engaging than the LLM chat format.</span></span>
<span id="A1.T8.4.6.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T8.4.6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">•I would prefer to use the slide-based format over the LLM chat format for learning new papers in the future.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Comparative Results.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Comparative Results. ‣ A.3. Slides vs. LLM Chat-based Learning ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> reports one-sample <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-tests of comparative ratings against the neutral midpoint, complementing the absolute ratings in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.3. User Study 2: Comparing Slides and LLM Chat-based Learning from Learners’ Perspective ‣ 4. Experiments ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> of the main text.</p>
</div>
