<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4. </span>Expert Evaluation of Narrative Structure Optimization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section expands on User Study 3 (§<a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. User Study 3: Evaluating Narrative Structure Optimization from Experts’ Perspective ‣ 4. Experiments ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>), where experts compared slides generated with and without PMRC-based narrative structure optimization.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Rubric.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Evaluation Rubric. ‣ A.4. Expert Evaluation of Narrative Structure Optimization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> lists all rubric items used for expert evaluations, covering <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Content Accuracy</em>, <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Information Density</em>, and <em id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Narrative Structure &amp; Flow</em>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10. </span>Evaluation rubric for creator study (7-point Likert scale: 1 = Strongly Disagree, 7 = Strongly Agree).</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T10.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T10.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
