<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6. </span>LLM-as-Judge Evaluation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of this evaluation was to measure the impact of:</p>
<ol id="A1.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the enhanced information extraction in the Parser Agent on <em id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Table &amp; Formula Fidelity</em>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the Verification–Adjustment Agents on <em id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Content Accuracy</em>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We provide explicit definitions, prompt templates, evaluation datasets, and full per-paper results to enable replication.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rating Scale and Aggregation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The comparative rating used a five-point ordinal scale:</p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">1 = “A is significantly better”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">2 = “A is slightly better”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">3 = “Tie”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">4 = “B is slightly better”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">5 = “B is significantly better”</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Forward and reverse judgments were collapsed into <em id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">win / tie / loss</em>.
Position bias was quantified as the percentage of forward–reverse disagreements.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Input Data and Preprocessing.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The content of each generated slide deck was converted to a structured JSON form prior to evaluation to remove any confounding visual or stylistic factors:</p><pre id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter">
{
  "slides": [
    {"slide_number": 1, "text": "..."},
    ...
  ]
}
</pre>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">LaTeX slides were parsed to:
(1) preserve mathematical formulas in original <span id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_LaTeX_logo" style="letter-spacing:-0.2em; margin-right:0.1em;">L<span id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:0.4ex;font-variant:small-caps;;">a</span>T<span id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.2ex;font-variant:small-caps;font-size:120%;">e</span>X</span>,
(2) convert tables into plain-text or Markdown representations,
(3) maintain figure/table references.
This ensures comparisons focus purely on content rather than formatting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Procedure.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the single-direction mode, Presentations A and B were loaded, prompts were generated by substituting the evaluation criteria and content, the LLM judge model was queried at temperature 0.0 for deterministic output, and the raw textual judgment was parsed.
In bidirectional mode, the evaluation was repeated with the order of A and B swapped; forward and reverse results were compared for agreement and collapsed to the final win/tie/loss label.
For <em id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Enhanced Content Accuracy</em> evaluation, the original paper text was also included in the prompt for factual verification.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Dataset.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used 14 academic papers from diverse technical domains (machine learning, computer vision, NLP) that contained substantial formulas and tables.
For each paper, we generated four presentation variants:</p>
<ol id="A1.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Original:</span> full <span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Auto-Slides</span> pipeline.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o InfoExt:</span> removal of enhanced information extraction stage in the Parser Agent.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o VerifLoop:</span> removal of the Verification–Adjustment Agents.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o NarOpt:</span> removal of the narrative optimization stage (exploratory).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Quality Control.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All generated decks were checked for successful compilation, and slide text was manually verified to avoid truncation before evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reproducibility Statement.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All prompt templates, rubrics, and preprocessing scripts are disclosed here for transparency.
Full data files and result artifacts will be made available in our public repository (link omitted for review) to support independent replication.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Human Validation of LLM-as-Judge.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the reliability of the LLM-as-Judge method, we conducted a human evaluation on a randomly selected subset of 5 papers from the <em id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Table Fidelity</em> condition.
Two Ph.D.-level researchers in HCI/CS, with no involvement in system development and blind to system identity, independently judged each Original <em id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">vs.</em> w/o InfoExt pair.
They were given the exact comparative evaluation prompt text described in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5. LLM-as-Judge Evaluation Materials ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Auto-Slides: An Interactive Multi-Agent System for Creating and Customizing Research Presentations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.
Raters used the same five-point comparative scale collapsed to win/tie/loss.
Agreement between the human majority vote and GPT<span id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>4o<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2024</a>)</cite> decision was <math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9/10</annotation></semantics></math> (90%).
Inter-rater agreement (<math id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0.82" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.82</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0.82</annotation></semantics></math><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen, 1960</a>)</cite>) indicated <em id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">almost perfect</em> agreement (Landis &amp; Koch, 1977<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Landis and Koch, 1977</a>)</cite>).
This high alignment suggests GPT<span id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>4o’s judgments were closely consistent with domain-informed human evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Full Results.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the complete per-paper forward and reverse results for each model and evaluation metric.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS0.Px8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Aggregated Forward/Reverse Statistics (Claude-3.7-Sonnet<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anthropic, 2024</a>)</cite>)</p>
</div>
